      "content": "it's just exhausting to \"just exist\" when existing feels like a chore. it's like you're just waiting for nothing to happen, but it's actually just more of the same nothingness. if nothing matters, then there's no real reason to stay in the cycle, right? it seems more like a surrender to reality than anything else. like, if everything is just a random accident, then choosing to leave the accident doesn't even matter either. it just feels like the only honest response to a void is to just... stop.",
